__d(function(e,o,t,s,h,r,a){h.exports={version:"2.0",board:"Karnataka State Board / NCERT",grade:6,subject:"English",textbook:"A Pact with the Sun",chapter_number:3,chapter_title:"The Shepherd's Treasure",total_cards:20,cards:[{id:"fc01",type:"Recall",difficulty:"Easy",front:"Who is the main character of 'The Shepherd's Treasure'?",back:"A young shepherd \u2014 a wise, kind, honest, and humble man who is known throughout the land for his good advice and help to others.",memory_hook:"Simple shepherd \u2192 wise governor. Humble origins, great character."},{id:"fc02",type:"Recall",difficulty:"Easy",front:"Why does the king summon the shepherd?",back:"The king hears that the shepherd is famous for his wisdom and kindness. He wishes to meet him personally.",memory_hook:"Good reputation travels. King heard of the shepherd \u2192 called him to court."},{id:"fc03",type:"Recall",difficulty:"Easy",front:"What does the king do after meeting the shepherd?",back:"He is so impressed by the shepherd's wisdom that he appoints him governor of a small district. Later, he promotes him to a larger district.",memory_hook:"Impressed king \u2192 small post \u2192 big post. Merit leads to promotion."},{id:"fc04",type:"Recall",difficulty:"Easy",front:"What object does the shepherd always keep with him?",back:"An iron chest \u2014 a strong, locked box that he never leaves behind.",memory_hook:"Iron chest = his most prized possession. Everyone is curious. What's inside?"},{id:"fc05",type:"Recall",difficulty:"Easy",front:"What do the jealous governors tell the king about the iron chest?",back:"They tell the king that the shepherd always carries a secret iron chest and suggest it might contain stolen treasure or gold.",memory_hook:"Jealousy makes up stories. 'Mystery chest = stolen goods!' \u2014 all lies."},{id:"fc06",type:"Recall",difficulty:"Easy",front:"What does the king do when he hears about the chest?",back:"The king summons the shepherd and orders him to open the chest in front of everyone at the court.",memory_hook:"Open it publicly = transparency test. Shepherd has nothing to hide!"},{id:"fc07",type:"Recall",difficulty:"Easy",front:"What is inside the iron chest?",back:"Only an old shepherd's cloak \u2014 the simple garment the shepherd wore when he was a poor shepherd.",memory_hook:"Expected: gold. Found: a worn-out cloak. The greatest surprise = simplicity."},{id:"fc08",type:"Concept",difficulty:"Easy",front:"Why did the shepherd keep an old cloak in the chest?",back:"The cloak reminded him of his humble origins. Whenever he felt too proud or important, he would put on the cloak to remember that he was once a poor shepherd. It kept him humble.",memory_hook:"Cloak = anti-arrogance medicine. Wear it when you feel too big for your boots."},{id:"fc09",type:"Definition",difficulty:"Easy",front:"What does 'humility' mean?",back:"Humility is the quality of not being proud or arrogant, even when you are successful. It means staying modest and grounded, remembering where you came from.",memory_hook:"Humble = grounded. Roots of a tree go deep \u2014 that's what keeps it standing tall."},{id:"fc10",type:"Definition",difficulty:"Easy",front:"What does 'integrity' mean? Give an example from the story.",back:"Integrity means being honest and doing the right thing, even when no one is watching. In the story, the shepherd had integrity \u2014 he could have filled his chest with gold as a governor, but he chose to keep only an old cloak.",memory_hook:"Integrity = doing right when no one sees. The shepherd had all the power and still chose honesty."},{id:"fc11",type:"Why/How",difficulty:"Easy",front:"How does the shepherd's explanation of the chest surprise the king?",back:"The king expected either stolen treasure or an embarrassing secret. Instead, the shepherd's explanation showed deep wisdom and self-awareness \u2014 that true greatness lies in humility, not wealth. The king was deeply moved and honoured the shepherd even more.",memory_hook:"Expected scandal \u2192 got wisdom. The king's jaw dropped (in admiration)."},{id:"fc12",type:"Concept",difficulty:"Easy",front:"What does the iron chest symbolise in the story?",back:"The iron chest symbolises the shepherd's humility and honesty. It is his real treasure \u2014 not gold, but the reminder to stay humble. It also symbolises the danger of jealousy, as others assumed the worst.",memory_hook:"Symbol = iron chest = humility. The chest is a mirror of his soul, not a bank vault."},{id:"fc13",type:"Application",difficulty:"Easy",front:"What is the moral of 'The Shepherd's Treasure'?",back:"Humility and honesty are a person's greatest treasures. True greatness comes from inner virtues \u2014 not from wealth, power, or status.",memory_hook:"Greatest treasure = inside you, not in a chest. Your character IS your gold."},{id:"fc14",type:"Definition",difficulty:"Easy",front:"What does 'jealousy' mean? How does it appear in the story?",back:"Jealousy is the feeling of wanting what someone else has, often leading to harmful actions. In the story, the other governors were jealous of the shepherd's success and tried to bring him down by falsely accusing him.",memory_hook:"Jealousy = trying to dim someone else's light. The governors couldn't stand the shepherd's shine."},{id:"fc15",type:"Why/How",difficulty:"Easy",front:"How did the shepherd survive the jealous governors' plot?",back:"He survived because he truly had nothing to hide. When the king ordered the chest opened, it contained only the cloak \u2014 proof of his honesty. Integrity was his best defense.",memory_hook:"Best defense against jealousy = nothing to hide. The shepherd was untouchable because he was genuinely clean."},{id:"fc16",type:"Recall",difficulty:"Easy",front:"What position does the shepherd finally hold by the end of the story?",back:"He is governor of a large, important district, highly honoured by the king \u2014 more than ever, after the king understands the meaning of the iron chest.",memory_hook:"Honest + humble = rises higher. Not despite his simplicity, but BECAUSE of it."},{id:"fc17",type:"Application",difficulty:"Easy",front:"What is your 'iron chest'? Think of something that reminds you to stay humble.",back:"Possible answers: A photo from when you first joined school, a letter from a teacher, a trophy that reminds you of hard work, or any object that keeps you grounded. The idea is the same as the shepherd's cloak \u2014 a reminder of who you are at your core.",memory_hook:"Your iron chest = your personal anchor. What reminds you of your true self?"},{id:"fc18",type:"Concept",difficulty:"Easy",front:"How does the story connect to Karnataka's cultural value of simplicity?",back:"Karnataka's saint-poets like Basavanna, Akka Mahadevi, and Kanakadasa all preached simplicity and humility over material wealth. The shepherd's story mirrors these values \u2014 true greatness comes from character, not status or riches.",memory_hook:"Basavanna said: 'Work is worship.' The shepherd's work was wisdom and service \u2014 not wealth-gathering."},{id:"fc19",type:"Why/How",difficulty:"Easy",front:"Why is the shepherd a good governor?",back:"Because he was kind, fair, wise, and honest. He had good judgment and genuinely cared about the people he governed. His qualities as a governor were an extension of his character as a shepherd \u2014 both roles required caring for others.",memory_hook:"Shepherd cares for sheep \u2192 Governor cares for people. Same character, bigger responsibility."},{id:"fc20",type:"Application",difficulty:"Easy",front:"Name three inner qualities the shepherd had that made him truly great.",back:"1. Humility \u2014 he never forgot where he came from. 2. Honesty/Integrity \u2014 he never misused his power. 3. Wisdom \u2014 he made good decisions and earned trust.",memory_hook:"H + H + W = Humility + Honesty + Wisdom = The Shepherd's Real Treasure."}]}},2941,[]);